# Inline Commands and Done State

## Semantic equivalence

In this app, **done** is represented consistently by:

- **Blue color** (e.g. `/blue`, `/ok`, `/done` inline commands)
- **Checked state** (`todo.checked === true`), same as when the user clicks the circle (see `checkTodo` in `todolist.store.js`)
- **Strikethrough** on the task title (UI applies this when `checked` is true)

So: done color, checked item, and strikethrough mean the same thing.

## Implementation rule

When an inline command sets the task to the **done** color (blue), the task must also be marked as **completed**:

- Set `todo.checked = true` (same behavior as `checkTodo` and `checkAllItems` in `todolist.store.js`).
- The store mutation `updateTodo` accepts optional `checked`; use it when applying the result of `processInlineCommands` if `result.checked === true`.
- In list view (`toDoItem.vue`): pass `result.checked` in the update payload, and when moving a task with done color set `toDo.checked = true`.
- In modal (`toDoModal.vue`): set `this.todo.checked = true` when `result.checked` is true before calling `updateTodo()`.

This keeps inline commands aligned with the rest of the app (checkbox, move-to-bottom for completed, etc.).
